To draw a chessboard based on a FEN notation using LATEX, you can use the `chessboard` package. Here's an example code:

```
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{xskak}
\usepackage{chessboard}

\begin{document}

\fenboard{rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 1}
\newchessgame

\begin{center}
\chessboard
\end{center}

\end{document}
```

In this example, we first load the `xskak` and `chessboard` packages. The `xskak` package is used to parse the FEN notation and set up the chess game. The `chessboard` package is used to draw the actual chessboard.

Then we use the `\fenboard` command to set up the board according to the FEN notation. We also use the `\newchessgame` command to initialize a new game.

Finally, we use the `\chessboard` command to draw the board in the center of the document. When you compile this code, you should see a chessboard with the starting position of a chess game.

